WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:03.968
- [Jason] Revelers in Times Square

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:06.750
on January 1st, 2020 expressed

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.021
the usual optimism about the new year.

00:00:09.021 --> 00:00:10.314
- This is our year.

00:00:10.314 --> 00:00:11.242
This is the world's year.

00:00:11.242 --> 00:00:12.657
- It's gonna be a great year.

00:00:12.657 --> 00:00:14.934
- Little did they know that
where they were standing

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:16.800
would, in just a few months,

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.229
due to the Corona virus
pandemic, become a ghost town.

00:00:20.229 --> 00:00:22.320
What a difference a year makes.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.780
This December 31st,
there'll be no crowds here

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.980
in Times Square as in so many
other cities around the world

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.184
that the pandemic is putting
a damper on celebrations.

00:00:31.184 --> 00:00:34.338
This year, the glimmering
crystal ball will still count

00:00:34.338 --> 00:00:36.611
the world down into a new year,

00:00:36.611 --> 00:00:38.500
but the hundreds of thousands of people

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.210
who normally line up the blocks
and brave the elements will

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:44.180
be reduced to a small
group of invited guests.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.347
- [Hosts] Three, two, one!

00:00:47.678 --> 00:00:49.095
- Happy new Year!

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:51.743
- [Jason] Carson Daly,

00:00:51.743 --> 00:00:53.460
who's been in Times
Square on New Year's Eve

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.688
for NBC since 2004, is adapting.

00:00:56.688 --> 00:00:58.930
- I don't think it's going
to be like happy new year,

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:00.060
it's two minutes away!

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.320
And all the, you know,
the background, obviously,

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:03.250
is going to be completely different.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:04.520
You know, usually if you
see me on Times Square,

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:05.740
you know, I'm like,
hey, where are you from?

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:06.573
Where are you from? Where are you?

00:01:06.573 --> 00:01:07.406
Oh, you drove from here?

00:01:07.406 --> 00:01:08.490
You flew from Peru, blah, blah, blah.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:09.894
It's so exciting here, guys.

00:01:09.894 --> 00:01:12.900
- [Jason] The tradition
of often-shivering crowds,

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.290
assembling shoulder to
shoulder in Times Square

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.918
to ring in the new year as
the ball drops dates back

00:01:17.918 --> 00:01:19.419
more than 100 years.

00:01:19.419 --> 00:01:22.623
There've been only two years
when the ball didn't drop,

00:01:22.623 --> 00:01:27.623
1942 and 1943, when the
ceremony was suspended due

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.940
to the wartime dim out of
lights in New York City.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.960
But this year, the show will go on,

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.620
staged for an at-home audience,

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.110
according to the president
of the Times Square Alliance,

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:39.561
which helps coordinate the event.

00:01:39.561 --> 00:01:43.200
- There will be a live
broadcast event in Times Square,

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.283
but there will not be a public audience.

00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:50.140
It will simply be a broadcast
stage for the entire world

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:50.973
to see.

00:01:50.973 --> 00:01:52.896
- [Announcer] Ring in a
year that has to be better.

00:01:52.896 --> 00:01:54.420
- [Jason] Broadcasters will be live

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.980
without the raucous crowds below.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:58.880
- Celebrate with us.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.670
- You sort of have to
kind of nail the tone

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:01.530
on a night like this,

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.870
because this has been just
a horrific year for so many,

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:04.868
because lives have been lost,

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:08.300
not to mention, if it wasn't
lives, it was livelihoods.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.655
So, and then there's some
people that, you know,

00:02:10.655 --> 00:02:12.300
may not have been affected.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.590
So, and everything in between.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:16.830
So, the tone, I think, is, is to be,

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:20.620
you know, optimistic and
hopeful, but reflective.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:22.557
- [Jason] The NYPD will
bar the general public

00:02:22.557 --> 00:02:26.100
from congregating anywhere
near Times Square.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.050
- The only people that
will be there besides

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:31.080
the performers will be about 40 people

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.238
who are our invited special guests.

00:02:33.238 --> 00:02:36.320
- In years past, the onstage production

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.440
featured special guests who
joined the mayor in pressing

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.828
the Waterford button that
triggers the ball drop.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:44.600
This year, first responders, frontline

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.022
and essential workers
will be the ones honored,

00:02:47.022 --> 00:02:49.850
but they'll remain in
socially-distant seating areas

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:50.805
with their families,

00:02:50.805 --> 00:02:53.870
rather than pressing the countdown button.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.850
The audience will also include
a small group of guests

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:58.160
who've rented, for the night,

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.230
this dome on NASDAQ's terrace,
overlooking Times Square.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:05.430
Airbnb, which debuted on
NASDAQ earlier in December,

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.720
says the guests who signed up

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.465
for this marketing gimmick are paying $21.

00:03:09.465 --> 00:03:12.120
New York isn't alone in finding ways

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.564
to adapt new year
celebrations to the pandemic.

00:03:14.564 --> 00:03:16.959
Some cities are canceling them altogether.

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:19.405
As Americans start the
day on December 31st,

00:03:19.405 --> 00:03:21.740
Sydney will kick off the new year

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:25.600
with a scaled down version of
its annual fireworks display.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.770
Hong Kong is doing away entirely
with its fireworks display

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.350
over Victoria Harbor.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.161
Officials say it's due to the pandemic.

00:03:32.161 --> 00:03:34.241
The government also canceled it last year,

00:03:34.241 --> 00:03:37.750
citing the threat posed by
antigovernment protesters.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:42.080
London, now in lockdown, has
canceled all public events,

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:43.595
including its firework show.

00:03:43.595 --> 00:03:47.090
And Las Vegas, which earlier
launched an ad campaign

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.638
to let people know it's open again,

00:03:48.638 --> 00:03:52.750
won't hold its annual
pyrotechnics display on the strip.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.136
Instead, the city is
promoting a virtual event

00:03:55.136 --> 00:03:58.615
where it plans to blow
up a 2020 sign, live,

00:03:58.615 --> 00:04:01.390
at an undisclosed location.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:02.280
Here in New York City,

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.558
where there've been around
20,000 deaths from COVID,

00:04:04.558 --> 00:04:07.242
the organizers of the event
say they want the tone,

00:04:07.242 --> 00:04:11.322
despite the pandemic, to
be celebratory and hopeful.

00:04:11.322 --> 00:04:14.090
- Staring at the ball,
being a part of such a rich,

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:17.728
American, iconic visual
of this ball dropping,

00:04:17.728 --> 00:04:21.160
I feel like will really
make people feel like, okay,

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.180
it's official now, it's 2021,

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.811
and a sense of relief,
and a sense of hope.

00:04:25.811 --> 00:04:28.016
- [Jason] And in a nod
to the year that was,

00:04:28.016 --> 00:04:30.388
two-time Grammy award
winner, Gloria Gaynor,

00:04:30.388 --> 00:04:31.620
will sing the lyrics.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.694
- Go on now, walk out that
door and just turn around now,

00:04:34.694 --> 00:04:36.160
you're not welcome anymore,

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.582
which I think is the way
we all feel about 2020.

00:04:38.582 --> 00:04:41.068
- [Jason] The message from
public officials worldwide,

00:04:41.068 --> 00:04:44.351
you can help make 2021 a year to celebrate

00:04:44.351 --> 00:04:46.845
by spending new years at home.

00:04:46.845 --> 00:04:49.345
(light music)

